    "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate reported a significant prior year reserve release of GBP 95.7 million in 2016, primarily driven by favourable claims development within the Energy and Treaty Divisions. This release represented approximately 5.9% of the opening gross claims outstanding. The report also detailed various catastrophe and large loss events in 2016, including earthquakes in Japan, Taiwan, Ecuador, Italy, and New Zealand, widespread floods in the US, China, and Europe, and the Fort McMurray wildfires in Canada. Specific large losses in the Marine XL account included the Samir refinery oil assets loss and the Amos 6 satellite explosion, while the Husky pipeline loss affected the Casualty division. Prior year events from 2015, such as the Tianjin explosion and UK floods, were also noted.",
